# Analects Book 12 (顏淵) — draft, first half: lemmata 0–28 = passages 12.1–12.11. Token format as the pilot:
#   tokens separated by " | "; a token is  CHARS[PUNCT][=pinyin][/context gloss[//char gloss//char gloss]]
#   a leading "^" breaks the verse line before the token.
# Punctuation is editorial (the edition has none) and always trails the word before it.
# Pinyin defaults to the glossary's first reading; every polyphone states its reading here, and so does
# every character not yet in the glossary (on every occurrence).
# Passages follow Zhu Xi's chapter breaks (凡二十四章): 12.1 = units 0–1, 12.2 = 2, 12.3 = 3–5, 12.4 = 6–7,
# 12.5 = 8–11, 12.6 = 12, 12.7 = 13–15, 12.8 = 16–18, 12.9 = 19–22, 12.10 = 23–25, 12.11 = 26–28.
# Quotation marks balance within every unit. Where a speech runs on past one of Zhu Xi's comments (12.5
# units 10–11, Zixia; 12.8 unit 18, Zigong; 12.10 units 24–25, the Master) the continuation is left
# unquoted, Chinese and English alike (as Books 8–11). The Ode lines in 12.10 (unit 25) carry no marks, as 9.30.
# Readings decided: 為 wéi throughout (0 ×2 'to practise', 5 'doing', 16 何以…為 final); 見 jiàn (2);
# 祭 jì (2); 語 yǔ (1, 2); 難 nán (5); 省 xǐng (7); 夫 fú (7, Zhu Xi 音扶); 夫子 fū zǐ (17, here Ji Zicheng);
# 亡 wú = 無 (8); 與 yǔ 'with' (11 與人, 22 孰與 ×2); 行 xíng (12 ×2, 'to get anywhere'); 遠 yuǎn (12, adj.,
# Zhu Xi marks nothing); 食 shí (13 'food', 15 'food', 28 'to eat'); 去 qù (14 ×2, 15 ×2; Zhu Xi 上聲 = qǔ,
# noted once at 14); 說 shuō (17, Zhu Xi marks nothing); 惡 wù 'to hate' (24, Zhu Xi 去聲); 祗 zhǐ (25:
# the edition's form of 祇 'only', Zheng Xuan 祗適也 — the glossary's 祗 entry, qí, needs zhǐ added);
# 齊 qí (26, state name); 訒 rèn (4, 5; Zhu Xi 音刃); 譖 zèn (12; Zhu Xi 莊蔭反, noted); 愬 sù (12; 蘇路反);
# 鞟 kuò (18; 其郭反); 已 yǐ; 大 dà (2, 大賓 大祭).
# Glyphs kept as printed: 顔 (0, 1), 徳 (23 ×2), 内 (7, 11), 鞟 (18 ×2), 祗 (25).
# Bound (keys exist): 顔淵, 天下, 仲弓, 君子, 兄弟, 子夏, 子張, 子貢, 夫子, 哀公, 如之何, 孔子.
# New bound keys needed: 司馬牛 (sī mǎ niú, the disciple; Zhu Xi 名犁, brother of 向魋), 四海 (sì hǎi, the four
# seas = the whole world), 棘子成 (jí zǐ chéng, a grandee of Wei), 有若 (yǒu ruò, = 有子), 百姓 (bǎi xìng,
# the hundred clans = the people), 齊景公 (qí jǐng gōng, Duke Jing of Qi, named 杵臼).
# New single characters needed: 克 kè, 兵 bīng, 崇 chóng, 愬 sù, 承 chéng, 景 jǐng, 棘 jí, 浸 jìn, 潤 rùn,
# 獨 dú, 疚 jiù, 膚 fū, 舌 shé, 訒 rèn, 誠 chéng, 譖 zèn, 豹 bào, 辨 biàn, 鞟 kuò, 駟 sì.
# Not bound, meaning what their parts mean: 克 | 己, 復 | 禮, 一 | 日, 大 | 賓, 大 | 祭, 不 | 敏, 死 | 生,
# 富 | 貴, 浸 | 潤, 膚 | 受, 虎 | 豹, 犬 | 羊, 孰 | 與, 崇 | 徳, 辨 | 惑, 而 | 已 | 矣.
# Collation (Ruan 1816 KR1h0004; He Yan SBCK KR1h0005): noted where sense-bearing — He Yan 其言也訒也 (4);
# He Yan 斯可謂之仁巳矣乎, Ruan 斯謂之仁已乎 (5); He Yan 斯可謂君子巳乎, Ruan 斯謂之君子已乎 (7); He Yan 皆爲兄弟也
# (11); 使民信之矣 (13); no 子貢, and 民不信不立 (15); 棘子城, 何以文爲矣 (16); 犬羊之鞹也 (18); 愛之欲其生也惡之欲其死也
